35", "SC-01", "CO-05", "AK-SEN", "MO-02", "FL-22", "OH-07", "OH-15", "IA-02", "AZ-02", "TX-SEN", "NY-17"], "sources": {"polls": 1886, "ratings": 2103, "markets": 709, "news": 3755, "fec_candidates": 1058}, "overview": {"summary": "The national environment strongly favors Democrats, with the generic ballot averaging a roughly nine-point Democratic lead across major pollsters in the final days. That margin is consistent with a substantial midterm wave, and both the quantitative outputs and prediction markets agree: the House is very likely to flip to Democratic control with a seat expectation in the mid-240s, and governorships are similarly likely to move Democratic. The Senate picture is more contested. Democrats are favored, with a mean expectation around 52 seats, but the margin between likely and unlikely control is narrower, and markets price Democratic control in the high-60s to low-70s. Competitive Senate races in Michigan, Texas, Ohio, Iowa, Maine and Nebraska remain genuinely close, and intraparty friction in Michigan adds late noise. A modest haircut to the generic ballot is warranted given typical late-cycle tightening, but the overall direction of the environment is clear.", "key_factors": ["Generic ballot shows a durable Democratic lead near nine points", "Quantitative model and prediction markets broadly agree on House and governor outcomes", "Senate control hinges on a handful of genuinely competitive states", "Late-cycle polling tightening risk typical of midterms", "Intraparty Democratic friction in Michigan adds uncertainty in a key race"], "chambers": {"house": "Democrats are strong favorites for House control, with the generic ballot, seat projections and markets all pointing to a majority in the mid-240s.", "senate": "Democrats are favored for Senate control with an expected 52 seats, but markets price it near 70 percent and several states remain genuinely competitive.", "governor": "Democrats are heavy favorites to win a majority of governorships, with an expected 28 to 29 seats and little downside risk."}, "environment_adjustment": -0.3, "uncertainty_multiplier": 1.0}}